    "title": "What channel is Arkansas vs High Point on today? Time, TV schedule for March Madness game",
    "text": "March 21, 2026, 4:02 a.m. CTPORTLAND, Ore. — Arkansas basketball's west coast journey in the NCAA Tournament continues today with a second-round matchup against High Point.A victory would send the Hogs a bit south to a Sweet 16 in San Jose, but they must first tackle a potential Cinderella.The No. 4 Razorbacks (27-8) face the No. 12 Panthers (31-4) on Saturday, March 21. High Point was the first underdog in this year's March Madness to spring a surprise when the Panthers toppled Wisconsin by one point for their first NCAA Tournament victory in program history.Arkansas followed that result inside with a 19-point thumping of Hawaii. Freshmen Darius Acuff Jr. and Meleek Thomas became the first freshmen duo in NCAA Tournament history to each score 20 points and dish out five assists in one game.This will be the second meeting between Arkansas and High Point. The Razorbacks cruised to an 89-48win in 2013 thanks to 16 points and nine rebounds by Bobby Portis.Here's a look at how to watch today's NCAA Tournament game between Arkansas and High Point.Watch Arkansas vs High Point on Sling TVWhat channel is Arkansas vs High Point on today in March Madness?TV channel: TBS or TRUTVStream: NCAA March Madness Live app | Sling TVThe Arkansas Razorbacks will tip off vs. the High Point Panthers on both TBS and TRUTV. Streaming options include the NCAA March Madness Live app and Sling TV, which offers a free trial. Announcers for the game are Brad Nessler and Wally Szczerbiak, with Jared Greenberg reporting from the sideline.Arkansas vs High Point start time in First Round of NCAA bracketDate: March 21Time: 8:45 p.m. CTThe Arkansas Razorbacks and High Point Panthers will play at 8:45 p.m. CT at the Moda Center in Portland Oregon. Local tip off is 6:45 p.m. PT.Jackson Fuller covers Arkansas football, basketball and baseball for the Southwest Times Record, part of the USA TODAY Network. Reach him at jfuller@usatodayco.com or follow him@jacksonfuller16 on X, formerly known as Twitter. Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
